Experiment No.: 12

Title

Interfacing PIR Sensor with Arduino

Aim

To interface a PIR sensor with Arduino for motion detection.

Theory

A PIR (Passive Infrared) sensor detects motion by sensing infrared radiation emitted by humans and objects.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
PIR Sensor
LED
Jumper Wires
Procedure
Connect PIR sensor output to Arduino pin 2.
Connect LED to pin 13.
Upload the program.
Move in front of the sensor.
Observe LED operation.
Code
int pir = 2;
int led = 13;

void setup()
{
  pinMode(pir, INPUT);
  pinMode(led, OUTPUT);
}

void loop()
{
  if(digitalRead(pir)==HIGH)
  {
    digitalWrite(led,HIGH);
  }
  else
  {
    digitalWrite(led,LOW);
  }
}
Output

LED glows when motion is detected.

Result

PIR sensor was successfully interfaced with Arduino.

Conclusion

Motion detection using PIR sensor was studied successfully.
